    <innerclass refid="classthemis_1_1server_1_1_http_shutdown_manager" prot="public">themis::server::HttpShutdownManager</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis">themis</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis_1_1server">themis::server</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Phased graceful-shutdown manager for the ThemisDB HTTP server. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements a well-defined, bounded multi-phase shutdown sequence:</para>
<para>Phase 0 – IDLE : Not yet initiated. Phase 1 – DRAINING : Acceptor closed; waiting for in-flight requests to complete within graceful_drain_timeout_ms. Phase 2 – FORCE_CLOSE : Drain deadline elapsed; any remaining requests are force-cancelled and their sessions closed. Phase 3 – TEARDOWN : All requests resolved; subsystems torn down. Phase 4 – DONE : Shutdown complete.</para>
<para>Design goals:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Thread-safe: phase transitions are atomic.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bounded: each phase has an explicit timeout; no phase can block forever.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Observable: phase transitions are logged and exposed via phaseLabel().</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No new allocations after construction.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>1.0.0 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Maturity: 🟢 PRODUCTION-READY </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Score: 93/100 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
